## 10. Case Study: What the Review Caught

Timeline of the confidential-rcv-template review (5 rounds, Jul 31 – Sep 2):

| Round | Finding | Fix |
|-------|---------|-----|
| 1 | 78-file vendored `ootle-rs` | `[patch.crates-io]` + submodule + upstream PR; dropped when upstream shipped |
| 1 | Hardcoded 10M publish fee (actual ~7.8M) | Size optimization + dry-run fee estimation |
| 1 | Hardcoded 50K call fee (~7x too high) | Dry-run fee estimation with 2x margin |
| 1 | Monolithic 346-line `main()` | Composable helper functions |
| 1 | Single-winner only; council needs N seats | STV + sequential IRV, method pinned at init |
| 1 | Happy-path tests only | 6+ adversarial tests with `execute_expect_failure` |
| 1 | Separate `initiate_vote` transaction | Merged into constructor (saves ~30s + one fee) |
| 2 | README falsely claimed it "extends" a sibling template | Removed stale claim |
| 2 | Decorative mint rule + `OwnedBySigner` = unlimited minting | `OwnerRule::None` + sealed NFT badge + locked updaters |
| 2 | Hardcoded initiator keys | Initiator = caller of `new()` |
| 2 | Six `end_vote*` variants enable result-shopping | Enum pinned at init, single `end_vote()` dispatch |
| 3 | Winner declared with zero ballots | `winner = None` on zero turnout (also fixed the Droop-quota-0 STV bug) |
| 3 | Dual cdylib+rlib silently disables LTO | Pure `cdylib` + tally extracted to standalone crate (314→248 KB) |
| 3 | Features-gated variants | Removed; one public template, config at init |
| Final | fmt/clippy | `cargo fmt`, clippy clean before merge |

