## 11. Publishing and Template Metadata

- **Web UI is the easiest publish path** (Estimate Fee → Publish), and `tari-ootle-cli` has a `tari publish` command. Programmatic publish is fine in clients **only with dry-run fee estimation** — never hardcoded amounts.
- **`tari publish` discovers `tari.config.toml` by walking up from the project dir.** Do not pass `-c tari.config.toml` — on `publish` that flag means `--custom-network`. Plain `tari publish` from the template directory is correct.
- **Templates explorer metadata** so your template shows up with docs:

  ```toml
  [package.metadata.tari-template]
  category = "governance"
  tags = ["voting", "governance", "dao"]
  docs = "https://..."
  homepage = "https://..."
  ```

  A `build.rs` using `tari_ootle_template_build` extracts per-method rustdoc into `template_metadata.cbor`, whose hash is registered on-chain at publish. Orphaned empty doc-comment lines break the extraction — keep doc comments tidy.

